**Motion findings:** motion instants — blade approach/contact ≈0–1000 ms · sawing (stop-motion steps, object rotating to horizontal) ≈1000–4000 ms · flesh extrusion onset bracketed between 2000 ms (absent) and 3000 ms (present) — i.e. flesh appears during the LATE saw, progressively, NOT only at completion · blade exit + closed-seam hold ≈4000–5000 ms. Holds — none long inside the window; the closing state (closed halves, green seam) holds at CP5 into the next technique. No dissolve; the substitution is covered by blade + hands throughout.
**Sub-beats:** SB-A present + blade approach (0–~1000 ms) · SB-B saw steps, shell only (≈1000–~2500 ms, flesh onset bracketed 2000–3000) · SB-C saw completion with progressive flesh extrusion (≈2500–4000 ms) · SB-D blade gone, closed halves with green seam, held (≈4000–5000 ms).

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Outer-object identity (CONFIG data): name, shell fill/highlight/shadow, segmentation columns × rows, body width/height, head (lever/pin) presence + colours — the thing being halved.
2. Inner-flesh identity (CONFIG data): name, flesh fill, flesh-light fill, skin-rim colour/width — what the cut reveals.
3. Blade: length, width, fill, edge colour, angle, travel distance, saw-step count, stroke amplitude (the back-and-forth inside each step).
4. Hands-as-shapes: grip shape fill (skin tone), size, positions (holder + guider), presence per phase.
5. Timing: present duration, saw start/duration, flesh-onset fraction of the saw, part/seam phase start/duration, hold, total duration.
6. Flesh geometry: extrusion width growth, seam-line width at close, flesh-face reveal fraction at part.
7. Ground/board: board fill, plank line colour/count, plate dressing presence (deferred — see §2.5).
8. Scale/position: object centre, object rotation (upright → horizontal tilt during saw), stage size.
9. Easing/step form: saw progress is STEPPED (stop-motion quantization), part phase eased.

### 1.5 Guidance dispositions (inline, A9.5)
- A1 §2 typography precedent: NOT APPLICABLE — no typography/particle text; the build carries no subject text at all.
- A5 Owner Cures 1–2: NOT APPLICABLE as particle/phrase cures — no particle field, no phrase lifecycle. The analogous separation here is identity-level: shell (dark, segmented) vs flesh (bright, smooth) are different kinds of mark by construction, never the same mark at two intensities.
- A5 §4 flow-field model: NOT APPLICABLE — no particle pool.
- A9.1 plate construction: the board is a STILL plate (flat ground + plank lines, no motion) — any background motion would exceed the technique; priced here so Plan-exit need not ask.
- Family: substitution-at-action siblings in Packet #13 — T232 (queue #103, this same wave) shares the spanning-action swap form; T234 (golf-ball lime) rides this same mechanism and is not owed separately (register-priced). No sibling scores exist yet (both first attempts this wave).

## §2 — PLAN

### 2.1 Parameter table (every variable → CONFIG key; specimen value = default)
`stageW 640 · stageH 400 · objCX 300 · objCY 205 · objW 190 · objH 230 · objTiltDeg -78 (saw-phase tilt; present phase 0) · segCols 4 · segRows 5 · segGroovePx 5 · headH 52 · bladeLen 300 · bladeW 64 · bladeAngleDeg -90 (edge vertical at contact, rotating with tilt) · bladeTravelPx 150 · sawSteps 5 · strokeAmpPx 14 · handW 150 · handH 110 · tPresentMs 0 · presentDurMs 900 · tSawMs 900 · sawDurMs 2600 · fleshOnsetFrac 0.62 · tPartMs 3500 · partDurMs 700 · partGapPx 10 · seamWPx 7 · holdMs 800 · palette {board #8a5a33, plank #6e4525, shell #44543c, shellLight #5c7050, shellDark #2e3a28, head #6b6f66, blade #b9bcbe, bladeEdge #e8eaea, hand #d9a184, flesh #7ec850, fleshLight #a8e063, skin #3d5a2a} · outer {name "grenade", shellKey "shell"} · inner {name "avocado", fleshKey "flesh"}` — identities are CONFIG DATA: `outer`/`inner` carry the names + which palette roles they bind; the swap test replaces the pair wholesale (see §2.4).
Derived (named, not stored): sawEndMs = tSawMs + sawDurMs · fleshOnsetMs = tSawMs + fleshOnsetFrac × sawDurMs (= 900 + 1612 = 2512 ms, inside the census bracket 2000–3000 ✓) · completeAtMs = tPartMs + partDurMs = 4200 · durationMs = completeAtMs + holdMs = 5000 = window ✓ · stepped saw progress = floor(sawP × sawSteps)/sawSteps with a within-step stroke oscillation of ±strokeAmpPx · flesh extrusion fraction = clamp01((sawP − fleshOnsetFrac)/(1 − fleshOnsetFrac)) during saw, then the part phase opens the seam to seamWPx and the flesh face shows between the halves. **Phase-order invariant (validation-enforced):** tSaw ≥ present end · fleshOnsetFrac ∈ (0,1) · tPart ≥ sawEnd · part end + hold = durationMs ≤ 5000 + handles.

### 2.2 Construction choice
**SVG scene, generated shapes only (chosen):** board rect + plank lines; the outer object as an SVG group — body ellipse clipped segmentation grid (segCols × segRows rounded cells drawn from CONFIG), head/lever shapes on top; the blade as a polygon; two hand shapes (rounded mitten paths) gripping object + guiding blade; the flesh as an extrusion blob path along the cut line (scaling with flesh fraction) + a seam ellipse revealed at part. All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node (A11 receipts). The object group rotates from upright (present) to horizontal (saw) per CONFIG tilt.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element measurement + DOM receipts. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function. Traced/photo assets — refusal class (§6.1), never considered as construction. HTML divs — SVG gives exact path geometry for harness receipts at less code.

### 2.3 Census-anchor mapping (A10.2) + A11 assertions
Window-start offset: segment-anchored, build 0 ms = source 9000 ms. NO departures: every census state maps to a CONFIG-expression probe at the same segment-relative instant.
Assertions (each: CONFIG expression → evaluated instant; all instants CONFIG-derived so a timing swap moves them — the T212 lesson applied at Plan, not discovered at prewave):
- CP0 zero: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tPresentMs)` → 0 ms: fleshFraction = 0, blade contact = 0, tilt = 0. (Zero-state anchor, guards cmd 8.)
- P1 contact: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSawMs)` → 900 ms: blade at contact (travelP = 0), flesh = 0, sawStep = 0.
- P2 mid-saw shell-only: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSawMs + CONFIG.sawDurMs/2)` → 2200 ms: sawP = 0.5 < fleshOnsetFrac → fleshFraction = 0; sawStep = floor(0.5 × sawSteps) = 2. (Census CP2 at 2000 ms is shell-only ✓ — probe sits inside the same census bracket.)
- P3 flesh onset: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSawMs + CONFIG.fleshOnsetFrac * CONFIG.sawDurMs)` → 2512 ms: fleshFraction = 0 at the onset boundary, > 0 immediately after (probe at +1 ms step in harness).
- P4 saw complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tSawMs + CONFIG.sawDurMs)` → 3500 ms: sawP = 1, fleshFraction = 1 (extrusion full), blade travel complete.
- P5 part complete: `stateAt(CONFIG, CONFIG.tPartMs + CONFIG.partDurMs)` → 4200 ms: seamGap = partGapPx, flesh face visible fraction = 1, blade withdrawn (bladeP = 0).
- P6 hold identity: `stateAt(CONFIG, completeAtMs + 400)` state fully equal to P5 state.
- **Fixed census-instant probes (C*, alongside — never the sole census assertions):** C@1000 — contact begun, flesh 0 (CP1). C@3000 — 0 < fleshFraction < 1 (CP3 extrusion in progress: at 3000, sawP = (3000−900)/2600 = 0.8077, flesh = (0.8077−0.62)/0.38 = 0.494). C@4000 — saw complete, part in progress (CP4). C@5000 — duration end state = P5 (CP5 closed seam hold).

### 2.4 Verification plan (instruments named)
- Execute checklist: (1) cut segment.mp4 from source.mp4 at 8.5–14.5 s (window ±0.5 handles), libx264/yuv420p + AAC faststart, ffprobe filed; (2) build recreation.html (CONFIG at top, pure stateAt, window.__T227 exposed); (3) build comparison.html (shared controls, video.currentTime − 0.5 s handle offset → build ms, labels as charged, phone stacking @media ≤560px); (4) own checks §5 legs 1–3.
